Full review comments:

- [P1] Require an admitted confidence review before switching to market — /home/drwho1985/workspace/algotradinglife/beijing-lot/quarto/fm171_full100_historical_20261018.qmd:43-44
  For the FM15 round, seven reconstructed markets pass these checks, but the frozen entries have no `review$confidence` or selection receipt; their reviews explicitly say `market_action='KEEP_NATIVE'`. This branch nevertheless selects market and claims a frozen uncertain-confidence rationale. Market sufficiency and consistency alone do not establish the inherited FM171 confidence gate. Require an explicitly bound qualifying confidence review, otherwise use a successful new native fit or mark the fixture unestimated.

- [P2] Validate cached model receipts before using reconstructed grids — /home/drwho1985/workspace/algotradinglife/beijing-lot/quarto/fm171_full100_historical_20261018.qmd:26-27
  Rendering loads the native and market RDS artifacts without independently replaying their receipts or checking their transitive implementation bindings. Only two native source hashes are checked; reconstructed markets are accepted here based on cutoff equality alone. Consequently, changing a bound market client, helper, source snapshot, or native implementation can still produce a fresh report using stale grids. Validate the stored bindings and replay the receipts before routing, failing closed on mismatches, as required by [AGENTS.md:131–137](../AGENTS.md#L131-L137).
